#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/business-logic.md
msgid "[Sasha Bespoyasov's notes on functional domain modelling](https://bespoyasov.ru/blog/domain-modelling-made-functional/) introduce domain language and boundaries. This guide applies that perspective to Jotai workflows; holo supplies bindings and ownership, not a domain architecture generator."
msgstr "[Sasha Bespoyasov's notes on functional domain modelling](https://bespoyasov.ru/blog/domain-modelling-made-functional/) introduce domain language and boundaries. This guide applies that perspective to Jotai workflows; holo supplies bindings and ownership, not a domain architecture generator."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/business-logic.md
msgid "Check a feature by asking: Can the View render with plain props? Can the business workflow run without analytics? Does each fact capture the context its consumers need? Is each subscription owned? Are Query and RHF adapters solving an actual atom-graph dependency? These questions matter more than using every operator."
msgstr "Check a feature by asking: Can the View render with plain props? Can the business workflow run without analytics? Does each fact capture the context its consumers need? Is each subscription owned? Are Query and RHF adapters solving an actual atom-graph dependency? These questions matter more than using every operator."

