#: docs/guide/motivation.md
msgid "Choose Jotai + holo when you want to change business rules without rewriting your React Views. Keep rules in atoms and models; connect small Views through ordinary props."
msgstr "Choose Jotai + holo when you want to change business rules without rewriting your React Views. Keep rules in atoms and models; connect small Views through ordinary props."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/motivation.md
msgid "Why Jotai?"
msgstr "Why Jotai?"

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/motivation.md
msgid "[Jotai](https://jotai.org/docs/basics/comparison) lets you compose state and calculations from atoms. A calculation can use another calculation without depending on a React component. This makes the same business logic available across the application."
msgstr "[Jotai](https://jotai.org/docs/basics/comparison) lets you compose state and calculations from atoms. A calculation can use another calculation without depending on a React component. This makes the same business logic available across the application."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/motivation.md
msgid "What does holo add?"
msgstr "What does holo add?"

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/motivation.md
msgid "holo describes the connection between a View and its atoms in one place. The View receives values and callbacks; the page composes connected components. Moving a component does not require forwarding its model's data through every parent."
msgstr "holo describes the connection between a View and its atoms in one place. The View receives values and callbacks; the page composes connected components. Moving a component does not require forwarding its model's data through every parent."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/motivation.md
msgid "Plain Jotai also supports this separation. holo provides conventions for bindings, model sharing and subscription cleanup, so each feature does not need to invent its own arrangement. Use it when you want the team to follow those conventions."
msgstr "Plain Jotai also supports this separation. holo provides conventions for bindings, model sharing and subscription cleanup, so each feature does not need to invent its own arrangement. Use it when you want the team to follow those conventions."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/motivation.md
msgid "Which approach fits your project?"
msgstr "Which approach fits your project?"

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/motivation.md
msgid "| Choose                                                       | When                                                                                           |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Jotai                                                        | You want atom-based state and prefer to connect components with native hooks.                  |\n"
"| Jotai + holo                                                 | You want atom-based business logic, separate Views and common conventions for connecting them. |\n"
"| [Effector](https://effector.dev/en/introduction/motivation/) | You prefer to build workflows around events, stores and effects.                               |\n"
"| [Reatom](https://reatom.dev/)                                | You want atoms, async operations and forms within one reactive ecosystem.                      |\n"
"| [React Hook Form](https://react-hook-form.com/)              | You need field state, validation and form submission.                                          |\n"
"| [Zag.js](https://zagjs.com/overview/introduction)            | You need ready-made state machines for accessible UI widgets, with your own markup and styles. |"
msgstr "| Choose                                                       | When                                                                                           |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Jotai                                                        | You want atom-based state and prefer to connect components with native hooks.                  |\n"
"| Jotai + holo                                                 | You want atom-based business logic, separate Views and common conventions for connecting them. |\n"
"| [Effector](https://effector.dev/en/introduction/motivation/) | You prefer to build workflows around events, stores and effects.                               |\n"
"| [Reatom](https://reatom.dev/)                                | You want atoms, async operations and forms within one reactive ecosystem.                      |\n"
"| [React Hook Form](https://react-hook-form.com/)              | You need field state, validation and form submission.                                          |\n"
"| [Zag.js](https://zagjs.com/overview/introduction)            | You need ready-made state machines for accessible UI widgets, with your own markup and styles. |"

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/guide/motivation.md
msgid "React Hook Form and Zag.js can be used together with holo. The [RHF integration](/topics/rhf-models) is useful when other atoms and models need access to form state."
msgstr "React Hook Form and Zag.js can be used together with holo. The [RHF integration](/topics/rhf-models) is useful when other atoms and models need access to form state."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
