msgstr "React-only throwOnError is unsupported. Enabled values, including inherited client defaults, fail explicitly during runtime initialization. Native factory types may widen this option, so validation occurs at runtime. Catch execution errors or read an error projection. Per-call mutate callbacks, cancellation, and automatic query invalidation are not added."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/createMutationModel.md
msgid "Use native useMutation when React owns the operation. Use createMutationModel only when the atom/model system needs to execute the mutation or react to its state. Several UI consumers alone do not require an atom adapter. Existing createMutationModel does not prevent native hooks elsewhere; shared mutation keys do not share an observer or execution state."
msgstr "Use native useMutation when React owns the operation. Use createMutationModel only when the atom/model system needs to execute the mutation or react to its state. Several UI consumers alone do not require an atom adapter. Existing createMutationModel does not prevent native hooks elsewhere; shared mutation keys do not share an observer or execution state."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/createMutationModel.md
msgid "atomWithMutation already integrates Jotai with TanStack. Our interface exposes a writable action directly and named projections instead of requiring callers to read a result atom to find mutate. This also makes it usable in holo.write and bond.write. Observing all mutations, including those launched by useMutation, is a separate cache-level task."
msgstr "atomWithMutation already integrates Jotai with TanStack. Our interface exposes a writable action directly and named projections instead of requiring callers to read a result atom to find mutate. This also makes it usable in holo.write and bond.write. Observing all mutations, including those launched by useMutation, is a separate cache-level task."

