#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/createQueryModel.md
msgid "- `state` accepts the same native atom, tuple, or record inputs as ion. All declared inputs are read when options are needed. The query factory receives their values.\n"
"- `query` returns complete native QueryObserverOptions. Pass your `gameDetailQO(params)` factory result unchanged. Keep keys, query functions, retries, and resource defaults in that factory. No Query Kit runtime is required.\n"
"- `prism` is an **object of independent selectors**. Unread selectors never execute. Equal selected results do not notify consumers, even if isFetching changes elsewhere in the result. A callback returning all fields is deliberately unsupported.\n"
"- `client` is your QueryClient or an atom containing it. Otherwise initialize [queryClientAtom](/reference/queryClientAtom) in the application's store. There is no hidden client. Share it with QueryClientProvider for native useQuery interoperability, and manage its application mount/unmount there."
msgstr "- `state` accepts the same native atom, tuple, or record inputs as ion. All declared inputs are read when options are needed. The query factory receives their values.\n"
"- `query` returns complete native QueryObserverOptions. Pass your `gameDetailQO(params)` factory result unchanged. Keep keys, query functions, retries, and resource defaults in that factory. No Query Kit runtime is required.\n"
"- `prism` is an **object of independent selectors**. Unread selectors never execute. Equal selected results do not notify consumers, even if isFetching changes elsewhere in the result. A callback returning all fields is deliberately unsupported.\n"
"- `client` is your QueryClient or an atom containing it. Otherwise initialize [queryClientAtom](/reference/queryClientAtom) in the application's store. There is no hidden client. Share it with QueryClientProvider for native useQuery interoperability, and manage its application mount/unmount there."

